{
  "id": "Compound::DB00331 - Gene::4698",
  "verbalization": "Metformin is shown to interact with Ndufa5 through a shared pathway involving Nadh Dehydrogenase (ubiquinone) or (quinone) activity. The evidence suggests that Metformin binds to Ndufa12 or Ndufv3, which are subunits of the Nadh Dehydrogenase complex, and that these subunits participate in the activity of the complex, which in turn is associated with Ndufa5. This indicates that Metformin may influence the function of Ndufa5 through a mechanism involving the Nadh Dehydrogenase complex. The high scores from the three paths suggest a strong and consistent relationship between Metformin and Ndufa5, likely mediated by the interaction with the Nadh Dehydrogenase complex. The mechanism appears to be biologically plausible, as the Nadh Dehydrogenase complex is involved in mitochondrial respiration and energy production, and Metformin is known to modulate mitochondrial function. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Metformin and Ndufa5, though further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the exact role of Ndufa5 in this process.",
